# function scale(list: number[], by: number) { for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i++) list[i] = list[i] * by; }
# What the loop stores may be a fraction, so its typed copy asks for double storage that may be written. A list that has held integers alone so far has int32 storage, and where the products stay whole it keeps it:
# the test would fail in front of every run of the loop, for ever, and all turns would run in the other copy. So a list that has int32 storage of its own is converted, once in its life, in front of that test:
# it passes, and the same run of the loop takes the typed copy. Converted behind the failed test, a fresh list paid the conversion and then the other copy over doubles, at every call.
# A front is three rows. Every list is asked whether it is as made: one that is not (an heir of Array) goes to the other copy as it is, and keeps its integers. Then the conversions. Then every list is asked for its kind of storage.
# No operation that changes a list may lie BETWEEN the tests for the kind: one list under two names could pass a test for int32 storage, be converted under its other name and pass the test for doubles:
# that one list cannot pass both is all that keeps two names apart: both(). That a list is as made holds across a conversion.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = IsPristine v0 builtinClass=Array
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch {{*}}notTaken [[other]]()
# CHECK: ConvertToDoubleStorage [[list]]
# CHECK-NEXT: [[holds]]: boolean @Boolean = HasArrayStorage [[list]] arrayStorage=Double [isWritable]
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch [[holds]] -> taken [[passed]](), notTaken [[other]]()
# CHECK-NOT: ConvertToDoubleStorage
# CHECK: PutDoubleIndex
# function both(read: number[], written: number[], by: number) { let sum = 0; for (let i = 0; i < written.length; i++) { sum += read[i] | 0; written[i] = written[i] * by; } return sum; }
# RUN(BOTH): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# BOTH-LABEL: code f3:Body
# BOTH: = IsPristine
# BOTH: = IsPristine
# BOTH: ConvertToDoubleStorage
# BOTH: = HasArrayStorage
# BOTH-NOT: ConvertToDoubleStorage
# BOTH: = HasArrayStorage
# BOTH: PutDoubleIndex
# RUN(COUNTED): compile ArraysConvertedToDoubleStorage mechanisms=all
# COUNTED: statistic ArraysConvertedToDoubleStorage 2
# A loop that only reads takes either kind and converts nothing: function sum(list: number[]) { let total = 0; for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i++) total += list[i]; return total; }
# RUN(READ): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# READ-LABEL: code f2:Body
# READ-NOT: ConvertToDoubleStorage
# RUN(SHELL): run-in-shell globalThis.sink = (...all) => { print(all.join(" ")); };
# SHELL: 6 2 4 6 12 1 2 3 6 0.5 1 1.5 3
# SHELL-NEXT: 6 6 2 0.5 1 3
# SHELL: exited with 0

